An anyOf union whose variants are not objects: null, an integer, a string,
an array of strings, a title-only variant, a $ref to a named string, and a
$ref to an enum. Each gets a constructor in its shape: one that takes the
value, converted to the variant's type, or one that takes nothing; and an
array variant holding nil is sent as []
(0014-MADR-union-constructors-take-every-required-key.md, V3, items 5 and 7).
The meta declares $/cancel_request and the schema its smallest definition,
which the runtime needs.

-- meta.json --
{"version": 1, "agentMethods": {}, "clientMethods": {}, "protocolMethods": {"cancel_request": "$/cancel_request"}}
-- schema.json --
{"$defs": {
  "Name": {"type": "string"},
  "Color": {"type": "string", "enum": ["red", "blue"]},
  "Val": {"anyOf": [
    {"type": "null"},
    {"title": "Count", "type": "integer", "format": "int64"},
    {"title": "Text", "type": "string", "minLength": 1},
    {"title": "Words", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}},
    {"title": "Marker"},
    {"$ref": "#/$defs/Name"},
    {"$ref": "#/$defs/Color"}
  ]},
  "CancelRequestNotification": {"type": "object", "x-side": "protocol", "x-method": "$/cancel_request"}
}}
-- want.api --
